# AdminV2 Runtime Performance (Protected Infrastructure)

AdminV2 loading and reveal behavior is **protected infrastructure**. The locked baseline is **`docs/system/adminv2-runtime-performance-doctrine.md`**.

Ownership migrations (QueueBlock → QueueRegion, compat work-unit page → WorkUnitSurface, drawer shell → AdminEntityDrawerLegacy): **`docs/platform/governance/runtime-ownership-migration-map.md`**.

## Before editing AdminV2 UI that touches drawers, queues, routes, tabs, layouts, or actions

1. Read `docs/system/adminv2-runtime-performance-doctrine.md`.
2. Treat the task as **UI-only** unless it explicitly says runtime/performance.
3. Do **not** modify runtime reveal gates during ordinary UI work.

## Hard rules

- Do **not** introduce section-owned above-fold skeletons.
- Do **not** treat unloaded queue state as empty (`queueRegionRenderState` must not show `"empty"` during cold load or refetch hold).
- Do **not** weaken composed payload readiness (`evaluateComposedDrawerPayload`, composed person payload).
- Do **not** remove request signature / stale-response apply guards (`queueRequestSeq` on work-unit queue fetch).
- Do **not** change cache keys without updating determinism tests.
- Do **not** clear valid displayed data before replacement is ready on warm navigation.
- Do **not** show false empty queue states while lane is cold-loading or holding prior rows.
- Prefetch is allowed; **partial above-fold reveal is not**.

## UI-only changes may alter

Spacing, typography, labels, section order (non-contract), visible fields, styling.

## UI-only changes may not alter

Payload readiness, request ownership, cache keys, stale guards, route/drawer reveal gates, queue empty semantics, known-empty predicates.

## Runtime-sensitive files (require test suite)

- `web/components/admin/AdminEntityDrawer.tsx` (shell router)
- `web/components/admin/AdminEntityDrawerLegacy.tsx`
- `web/components/admin/entity/*Drawer*`
- `web/components/admin/opportunity/*`
- `web/components/presentation/workUnit/WorkUnitSurface.tsx`
- `web/components/presentation/workUnit/QueueRegion.tsx`
- `web/lib/presentation/runtime/useWorkUnitSurfaceRuntime.ts`
- `web/lib/admin/drawer/composedDrawerPayload/*`
- `web/lib/admin/drawer/*Reveal*`
- `web/lib/adminV2/runtime/contract/*`
- `web/lib/workspace/*Queue*`
- `web/lib/admin/opportunityDrawer*`
- `web/lib/admin/prefetchPersonDrawerSnapshot.ts`

## Required tests when touching runtime-sensitive files

```bash
cd web && npm run test -- \
  tests/admin/drawer/drawerDeterminism.test.ts \
  tests/admin/drawer/composedDrawerPayload.test.ts \
  tests/admin/drawer/drawerAboveFoldCoordinatedReveal.test.ts \
  tests/admin/drawer/opportunityDrawerHeaderActionsRestore.test.ts \
  tests/adminV2/workUnitQueueLaneRevealState.test.ts \
  tests/adminV2/workUnitPageRevealPolicy.test.ts \
  tests/adminV2/workUnitCoordinatedRevealRegression.test.ts \
  tests/lib/workspace/routeSessionCacheAndReveal.test.ts
```

Also run `cd web && npm run typecheck` before merge on TypeScript changes.
